&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer Rotational Program – Early Career&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About InterSystems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InterSystems powers mission-critical applications in healthcare, financial services, government, and other industries. Our data platform, interoperability solutions, and analytics technologies help organizations solve complex problems and deliver meaningful outcomes. With a focus on innovation and client success, we support systems that make a real-world impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;strong&gt;Core Development Program&lt;/strong&gt; is a rotational experience designed specifically for students graduating in Fall 2026 or Spring 2027 (BS, MS, or PhD) who are looking to build a strong foundation in software engineering. The program offers opportunities in front-end, back-end and/or full stack development across our product teams. You’ll contribute to real codebases and collaborate cross-functionally gaining exposure to a wide range of technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Highlights:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3-week onboarding and training:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn core technologies, tools, platforms, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two 6-week team rotations:&lt;/strong&gt; Complete two 6-week software development projects with different InterSystems product teams (HealthShare, IntelliCare, Data Platforms, Financial Services).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship and support:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with experienced engineers for guidance and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team placement:&lt;/strong&gt; After successful completion of the program, participants who have met InterSystems’ expectations during their rotations will transition to their long-term role with a team based on interest, fit, and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Team Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Gain experience working on interoperability platforms, data infrastructure, and clinical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supportive Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn from seasoned engineers with insight into best practices and career planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career Path:&lt;/strong&gt; Transition into a full-time role with growth opportunities in software development and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graduating in Fall 2026 or Spring 2027 with a degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, or a related STEM field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with at least one programming language (e.g., JavaScript, Python, Java, C++, C#).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of data structures, algorithms, and object-oriented programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI/agentic tools and their applicability to software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eagerness to learn new tools, technologies, and domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiative shown through personal, academic, or team projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
