&lt;p&gt;InterSystems Corporation, a leading developer of data platform and interoperability technologies, is seeking candidates for its U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) Account Team. The “Enterprise Solutions Advisor - VA” role is client-facing, fast-paced, wide-ranging and challenging. It requires a mixture of application development and deployment skills, hands-on coding and problem-solving, presentation skills, sales awareness, implementation and project management awareness, and clinical and business acumen. Occasional regional travel is a requirement for the role. &lt;em&gt;This role is critical to InterSystems’ success within the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, serving as a trusted technical advisor and strategic partner to ensure successful adoption and expansion of InterSystems technologies across the VA ecosystem.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating with InterSystems&#39; VA Account Representatives and all other departments within InterSystems to ensure a close, long-term, and responsive relationship with the VA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted technical advisor to VA stakeholders and own technical relationships across the VA account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for successful technical adoption and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving successful VA outcomes and long-term value with InterSystems technologies in use within the VA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide architectural and strategic technology decisions within the VA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with System Integrators and Project Managers within the VA, especially during the early stages of adoption and technically challenging projects, to ensure successful implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommending technical architectures, model design, development patterns, migration strategies, upgrade procedures, and operational best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and presenting Proofs of Concept (PoCs) for the VA and their partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering standard and customized on-site training in a classroom environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the VA and their partners during beta test programs or pre-launch activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting marketing activities at trade shows, conferences, seminars etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping up-to-date with InterSystems products and contemporary IT industry developments (including competitive products) and undertaking any relevant self-development or training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating prototypes and coordinating with product management to enhance product offerings based on client desires/needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing competitive proposals, solution overviews, sales collateral, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting technical and non-technical issues related to the VA to the appropriate InterSystems departments, and overseeing resolution to those issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success Criteria:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful deployment and adoption of InterSystems solutions within VA programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical relationships with VA and system integrators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expansion of use cases and footprint within the account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive VA feedback and reference-ability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence on InterSystems product direction based on VA needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in software engineering role(s), with 5+ years of experience as a Technical Account Manager and/or Solution Consultant, with preference for U.S. Government experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with government security standards (FedRAMP, FISMA, etc.) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awareness of data privacy, security, and compliance requirements in healthcare and public sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle technical questions and provide solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in architecture design and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with most/all of the following
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Object-Oriented Programming and/or Enterprise Application Development, vibe coding, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relational or non-relational databases using SQL or NoSQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Engineering skills using Python, GenAI, RAG, MCP, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern Analytics architectures - Data Lakes /Data fabrics/Data mesh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine Learning and Generative AI use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTML, JavaScript, Angular&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;XML, XSLT, JSON, SOAP, REST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud hardware services, containers, kubernetes, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Windows, Unix/Linux, MAC OS X&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare Interoperability Standards and Protocols (FHIR, HL7v2, CCD/CCDA, X12, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the VistA Electronic Medical Record is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted tools (e.g. copilots, summarisation tools, or chatbots) with an ability to critically evaluate and verify AI-generated outputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to learn, evaluate, adapt to, propose and implement AI-augmented workflows in order to continually enhance your own, and the team’s productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication Skills&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills to interact with a wide range of stakeholders, including clinicians, C-level executives, and software engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to deliver compelling presentations and product demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solving Skills&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills to assess technical feasibility and recommend strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead and manage Proof of Concept (POC), Prototype, and Paid Pilot projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
