&lt;h2&gt;Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We are seeking a Kubernetes Developer to join our global infrastructure and platform engineering team, helping build software-driven automation for InterSystems Kubernetes-based managed services and SaaS platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You will work with software engineers, Kubernetes architects, DevOps, SRE, and security teams to develop reliable, secure, production-ready platform capabilities. The role combines Go development with hands-on Kubernetes experience, with a focus on turning repeatable operational processes into maintainable platform software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Kubernetes-native software in Go, including controllers, Custom Resource Definitions (CRDs), reconciliation logic, and automation components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation for provisioning, configuration, upgrades, scaling, recovery, and other managed service workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write maintainable Go code and develop unit, integration, and cluster-based tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support CI/CD pipelines for building, testing, packaging, and releasing Kubernetes platform software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with Kubernetes networking, storage, ingress, certificates, scheduling, security, and cluster lifecycle capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to automation using Helm, Terraform, GitOps, Argo CD, Flux, and related tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement secure defaults, least-privilege RBAC, secrets handling, workload isolation, and operational guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build observable and supportable software using logs, metrics, events, health checks, and status conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot Kubernetes workloads, controller behaviour, failed reconciliations, deployments, and automation issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, SRE, security, and application teams, and contribute to documentation, runbooks, and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in software engineering, platform engineering, DevOps, infrastructure automation, cloud engineering, or SRE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing in Go, or strong software engineering experience with the ability to work in Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with Kubernetes, containers, Linux, and cloud-native deployment patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Kubernetes APIs, CRDs, controllers, reconciliation loops, RBAC, events, status conditions, and resource lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git, CI/CD, automated testing, and code review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Helm, Terraform, GitOps, Argo CD, Flux, or similar tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Kubernetes security concepts including RBAC, secrets, namespaces, network policies, admission controls, and workload isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, communication, and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubebuilder, Operator SDK, controller-runtime, client-go, or similar frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing Kubernetes Operators, controllers, admission webhooks, or platform automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with EKS, AKS, GKE, Rancher, Spectro Cloud, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Fluent Bit, ELK/EFK, Istio, Linkerd, Cilium, Velero, Kasten, or Stash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open-source contributions to Kubernetes, Go, cloud-native, or platform engineering projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as CKAD, CKA, CKS, Terraform Associate, or LFCS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
