&lt;p&gt;InterSystems is seeking a Senior Advisor, Healthcare Delivery, North America IDNs / Providers to join our Global Healthcare Market Strategy team. This senior-level individual contributor will own the market narrative, drive thought leadership and industry engagement, and ensure InterSystems maintains sustained visibility, credibility, and influence in the North American provider ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Market Strategy role within Marketing. The Senior Advisor partners closely with Product, Sales, Customer Success, and Product Marketing to translate provider / IDN market needs into clear strategy, messaging, Sales enablement, and market-facing programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a healthcare operational leader with deep understanding of how large IDNs and health systems operate who has or has had direct expertise in provider operations, health system strategy, IDN decision-making, enterprise priorities, and the operational realities that shape technology adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InterSystems has been a leader in data management, interoperability, and digital health since its inception. Today, more than 1 billion health records worldwide are managed using InterSystems technology, including HealthShare, InterSystems IRIS for Health, InterSystems IntelliCare, and TrakCare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This new role will focus initially on North America, with the potential for limited international work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market strategy and positioning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the segment expert for North American IDNs, health systems, and provider delivery organizations within Market Strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain the provider / IDN positioning, messaging, and narrative in partnership with Product Marketing and Product Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide continuous market analysis on IDN priorities, including operational performance, access, capacity, workflow burden, care coordination, interoperability, data platforms, AI readiness, modernization, cost pressure, and quality improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate provider-market insights into practical guidance for go-to-market strategy, Product direction, Sales enablement, and executive-level messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help InterSystems identify where it has a credible and differentiated role in supporting large provider organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provider operations and IDN market expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring deep understanding of how large provider organizations operate, make decisions, fund initiatives, adopt technology, and measure value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise internal teams on IDN operating models, executive priorities, buyer personas, governance structures, procurement dynamics, and implementation realities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect provider operational pressures to technology-enabled opportunities, including data strategy, interoperability, analytics, workflow integration, care coordination, enterprise modernization, and AI readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help InterSystems understand what provider executives need, what problems they are trying to solve, and what proof points are required to create credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry engagement and market influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and sustain senior relationships with key provider / IDN leaders and influential industry stakeholders, including COOs, CIOs, CMIOs, CDOs, chief transformation officers, digital leaders, operational leaders, and innovation executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build InterSystems’ provider / IDN market credibility through conference presence, webinars, speaking, writing, media engagement, executive forums, and strategic participation in high-impact industry venues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where InterSystems should show up, what conversations we should lead, and which relationships or events matter most for provider-market credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent or coordinate representation for InterSystems in relevant industry forums and communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyst engagement and relationships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute provider-segment analyst engagement in partnership with Marketing and Product leaders, including analyst briefings, inquiry preparation, narrative alignment, and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain trusted relationships with key analysts covering provider IT modernization, interoperability, data platforms, digital health, AI readiness, and enterprise healthcare technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure InterSystems’ provider narrative is consistently understood, differentiated, and accurately reflected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional internal leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic SME leadership to Product, Product Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and leadership teams on provider-market dynamics, IDN priorities, buyer personas, and competitive context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Enablement to translate positioning into usable field assets, including talk tracks, discovery questions, objection handling, proof points, and executive-level messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create feedback loops from the field, customers, prospects, and industry engagement into Product and Marketing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help Product and Product Marketing connect provider-market needs to InterSystems capabilities, roadmap considerations, use cases, and value propositions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer and partner advocacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop customer stories, references, proof points, and speaking opportunities, especially within IDNs, large health systems, and complex provider organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic customer and prospect conversations where provider operational expertise is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support partner alignment where provider / IDN ecosystem relationships are required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help translate customer and partner insights into actionable recommendations for Product, Sales, Marketing, and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of relevant healthcare experience, including significant experience working within large provider organizations, IDNs, health systems, or complex delivery networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in provider / IDN operations, enterprise priorities, buying dynamics, decision-making structures, and technology adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the operational, financial, workforce, workflow, quality, access, capacity, and modernization pressures facing large health systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging senior provider executives, such as CIOs, COOs, CMIOs, CDOs, chief transformation officers, digital leaders, enterprise operations leaders, or clinical operations leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect provider operational challenges to technology strategy, including data platforms, interoperability, analytics, digital transformation, workflow integration, enterprise modernization, and AI readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the provider healthcare IT landscape, including EHR ecosystems, interoperability, data strategy, analytics, and emerging AI-related needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, including executive presence, public speaking, writing, and the ability to translate complex market dynamics into clear, practical recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in-office in Boston, MA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with interoperability and healthcare data standards and the role of standards in market adoption, including awareness of HL7®, FHIR®, and the broader standards ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence and align cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing go-to-market strategy, Sales enablement, Product strategy, market positioning, analyst engagement, or thought leadership for provider audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree preferred, such as MBA, MHA, MPH or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
