&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Role Overview&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and proactive Senior Contracts Manager to join the UKI Legal team. The role will support business growth and financial objectives by managing legal and commercial risk and enabling effective delivery of software and services to the NHS, and other UK &amp;amp; Ireland (UKI) healthcare and non-healthcare customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Contracts Manager will play a key role in managing contracts across their full lifecycle, working closely with the Legal, Sales, Delivery and Leadership teams to ensure contractual arrangements align with business objectives, governance requirements and public sector procurement norms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the senior contracts role in the UKI Legal team, the Senior Contracts Manager will generally be assigned the most complex, high-value and strategically significant matters. They must also operate with substantial autonomy within an agreed mandate, and help set standards, draft regional and global processes, and develop capability across the contracts function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be based in either InterSystems’ Windsor, Edinburgh, or Dublin offices and may require occasional domestic and international travel. Office location will be determined based on the successful candidate’s location. An office location that is not Windsor will require periodic attendance at the Windsor office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Responsibilities &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;– The role encompasses end-to-end contract lifecycle management, including pre-contract support, post-contract management, and risk and governance oversight.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pre-Contract Activities&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead legal team input into assigned tender and bid responses, particularly for NHS and other public sector procurements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review and negotiate a range of customer and supplier contracts, ensuring alignment with business objectives, legal and commercial risk appetite, and applicable NHS and public sector requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide pragmatic and commercially focused contractual advice to support sales and project mobilisation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Post-Contract Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take named, end-to-end ownership of a defined portfolio of client contracts, including high-value and complex contracts, holding accountability for commercial outcomes across the contract lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contracts following signature, including business adherence to contractual obligations, change control processes and contract variations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the delivery and operations teams in the practical application and management of contractual obligations throughout the contract lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor contractual performance, compliance and key post-signature obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management of third-party vendors/sub-contractors and suppliers, both local and global, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Risk and Governance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the implementation, day-to-day governance, administration and continuous improvement of regional and global AI-enabled legal support technologies, ensuring effective, compliant and business-aligned usage across the legal function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, assess and escalate legal and commercial risks to appropriate internal stakeholders and, where necessary, internal or external legal counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and ensure adherence to internal contract management and governance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage ambiguity and develop practical, proportionate solutions to contractual and risk management challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Stakeholder Engagement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear, practical guidance on contractual matters to colleagues at all levels, including the Legal, Sales, Delivery and Leadership teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop contract managers and other colleagues, setting standards and sharing best contract management practice across the global legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with local and international colleagues to resolve contractual issues efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Experience/Qualification Required &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 7-9 years proven, hands-on experience in high-value contract management, ideally within healthcare, IT, and/or the public sector. As a guide to applicants, evidence of a directly accountable portfolio TCV over £100M is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of operating with autonomy on high-value, complex and strategically significant contracts, and of leading negotiations through to conclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong drafting, negotiation and analytical skills, with a pragmatic and commercially focused approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with digital workflow tools, document automation systems, and AI enabled legal support technologies to improve contract review speed, accuracy, consistency, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of legal operations processes, contract lifecycle management platforms and AI-enabled legal technologies is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience of using UKI model form contracts and frameworks, with an understanding of government and NHS procurement laws and public sector contracting norms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify, define and articulate key commercial principles to support sound legal and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to explain complex contractual issues to non-specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, strong organisational skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree and/or postgraduate qualifications with a legal or commercial focus are preferred; relevant professional qualifications are welcomed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-related regulatory environments such as the EU AI Act is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About InterSystems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;InterSystems, a creative data technology provider, delivers a unified foundation for next-generation applications for healthcare, finance, manufacturing, and supply chain customers in more than 80 countries. Our data platforms solve interoperability, speed, and scalability problems for large organizations around the globe to unlock the power of data and allow people to perceive data in imaginative ways. Established in 1978, InterSystems is committed to excellence through its 24×7 support for customers and partners around the world. Privately held and headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts, InterSystems has 38 offices in 28 countries worldwide. For more information, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https://www.intersystems.com/&amp;amp;esheet=53379223&amp;amp;newsitemid=20230410005415&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=InterSystems.com&amp;amp;index=4&amp;amp;md5=3edf749fa33f5a2ac0c355c410576e90&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;1e721f69-f681-4067-9281-970e94b3ef11&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;InterSystems.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Disclaimer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;InterSystems may use AI tools for its internal operations including administrative tasks during recruitment (e.g., organizing candidate information). &amp;nbsp;InterSystems’ approach to AI is guided by the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.intersystems.com/ai-use-guidelines/&quot;&gt;InterSystems Responsible AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;. AI is not used to make or influence hiring decisions. All decisions are made by InterSystems employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates may use AI for CV or interview preparation, provided materials are truthful and reflect their own experience. &amp;nbsp;AI tools and third-party transcription services must not be used during interviews or assessments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that the use of wearable technology, including any AI-related tools or other technology-connected devices (such as META or Google smart glasses and/or wearables, and/or any similar devices), is&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;strictly prohibited&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;during the interview and screening process with InterSystems.&amp;nbsp; Any applicant who requires a wearable device or any type of technology support during the interview process as a reasonable accommodation under the ADA or applicable state or country laws and regulations must contact the InterSystems Human Resources Department&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;prior&lt;/em&gt; to attending or participating in any interview or screening process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our Hosting team delivers InterSystems&#39; solutions as hosted or managed services to customers worldwide, supporting business-critical and regulated workloads that require dependable protection and recoverability. The annual goal of this role is to implement and operate consistent global data protection practices, policies, and services using Rubrik Enterprise Edition. The role holder will strengthen backup, recovery, cyber resilience, and governance while improving automation, assurance, and operational maturity. Success is measured by policy compliance, protection coverage, recovery readiness, service reliability, reduced data-loss risk, and demonstrable achievement of recovery objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Regional Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global scope on an enterprise data protection platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer Rubrik Enterprise Edition across business-critical environments and establish consistent protection and recovery practices worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to shape global data protection standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence decisions covering policy design, retention, recovery, cyber resilience, automation, and the long-term direction of data protection services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive compensation and benefits package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A competitive package with market-aligned compensation and comprehensive benefits for a senior technical role based in Dublin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful work supporting healthcare customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect systems and data used by clinicians and care providers, helping ensure that critical services can be recovered reliably when customers need them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within a skilled, collaborative engineering and architect teams&lt;br&gt;Join a global hosting and infrastructure team that values shared ownership, operational excellence, continuous improvement, and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement, administer, and improve Rubrik Enterprise Edition globally, including configuration, upgrades, capacity, health, security, and lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce global data protection policies, SLA domains, retention standards, archival, replication, immutability, access controls, and encryption requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business, regulatory, contractual, and risk requirements into protection tiers, recovery point objectives, recovery time objectives, and operating procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboard workloads to the protection service and maintain accurate coverage across supported on-premises, cloud, virtual, database, and application environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and monitor backup, replication, archival, and recovery; resolve job failures, capacity constraints, policy exceptions, and performance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute restore tests, disaster recovery exercises, and readiness reviews, maintaining evidence that recovery objectives and controls are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cyber recovery and ransomware resilience, including anomaly investigation, clean recovery planning, privileged-access controls, and coordination with security and incident response teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish procedures, runbooks, standards, and governance for data protection services, and drive consistent adoption across regions and technology teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to data protection incidents and service degradation, lead technical troubleshooting, and contribute to root cause analysis and corrective and preventative actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate operations, compliance checks, reporting, and workflows using Rubrik APIs and appropriate scripting or orchestration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on protection coverage, recoverability, policy compliance, capacity, platform risk, and operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with infrastructure, cloud, database, application, security, risk, and business continuity teams; participate in a shared on-call rota for critical production services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience / Qualifications Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience engineering and operating enterprise-scale backup, recovery, and data protection services. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on production experience with Rubrik Enterprise Edition. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Rubrik Certified System Administrator (RCSA) certification is required. Rubrik Certified Engineer (RCE), Rubrik Certified Cloud Specialist (RCCS), or Rubrik Partner Black Belt is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equivalent current Rubrik credentials demonstrating advanced implementation, cloud-protection, or cyber-recovery expertise will also be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and implementing global data protection policies, standards, and operating models. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of retention, immutability, encryption, access control, RPO, RTO, and recovery validation. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting disaster recovery, cyber recovery, or ransomware-resilience capabilities. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven troubleshooting skills and experience working within incident, change, and problem management processes. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting production services in a 24x7 or on-call environment. - Essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience protecting VMware, Nutanix, Windows, Linux, database, and cloud workloads. - Preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using APIs, scripting, or automation tooling to operate data protection services at scale. - Preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting audit, risk, compliance, and customer assurance activities. - Preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About InterSystems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
