&lt;p&gt;The Facilities Team at InterSystems is a dynamic department that handles requests and maintenance across the entire company. We are currently searching for a proactive individual to join the group to help coordinate daily efforts.&amp;nbsp; The Facilities Assistant reports directly to the Facilities Supervisor and assists the Facilities Department with general operations of over 360,000ft² of commercial Class A office space located at the world headquarters in Boston, MA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct daily facility inspections to identify safety, maintenance, cleanliness, and operational issues and ensure a safe, clean, and productive work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and manage corrective and preventive work orders, including follow-up with internal staff, building management, vendors, and contractors to ensure timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships and day-to-day coordination with building ownership/management, security, janitorial services, parking, engineering, and outside contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage facility-related vendor services and contracts, including scheduling, performance monitoring, issue resolution, and invoice review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate facility records, documentation, floor plans, equipment information, maintenance records, work requests, shipping/receiving records, and other operational documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate facility projects, repairs, renovations, office moves, employee workspace setups, and other workplace changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and interpret basic construction drawings, floor plans, and MEP documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support building operations and maintenance activities, including coordination with building engineering and property management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Security and Fire/Life Safety programs, inspections, testing, and emergency preparedness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and support access control, video conferencing, phone systems, and other workplace technology as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of contact for employees, vendors, contractors, building management, ownership, and senior management regarding facility-related matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide facility support before, during, and after critical incidents and emergency events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate workplace services including meeting preparation, conference rooms, food services, parking, vending, site access, and other employee amenities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and support corporate events, including events occurring outside normal business hours or at off-site locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the development and management of facility operating budgets, review expenses, monitor vendor costs, and identify opportunities for cost savings and operational efficiencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain effective working relationships with Administration, Marketing, Finance, Human Resources, IT, Security, and other departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a professional, service-oriented approach when interacting with employees, vendors, contractors, building management, and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&amp;nbsp;preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive experience in commercial property management, facilities management, building operations, or a related field preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of building systems, including HVAC, electrical, plumbing, life safety, and other MEP systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of commercial office building operations and property management practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, communication, problem-solving, and customer-service skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid, clean driver’s license in Massachusetts is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position requires exerting up to 40 pounds of force in order to lift, carry, pull or remove objects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge in Microsoft Office (specifically Excel and Word).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work flexible hours, and weekends if needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
